  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0f3a2c8c7b8f4d9c9d5a3d11d5f50101, type: 3}
  m_Name: PokedexScorpion
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryId: scorpion
  commonName: Deathstalker Scorpion
  scientificName: Leiurus quinquestriatus
  icon: {fileID: 10904, guid: 0000000000000000f000000000000000, type: 0}
  category: Arachnid
  habitat: Arid Deserts & Scrublands
  height: 8 - 11 cm
  weight: 1 - 2.5 g
  diet: Carnivore
  rarity: Rare
  shortDescription: A highly venomous, desert-dwelling arachnid with a pale, straw-colored
    body, slender pincers, and a fast-striking stinger.
  behaviorNotes: Primarily nocturnal, hiding under sun-baked rocks or deep within
    sand burrows during the daytime to regulate moisture. They hunt by waiting completely
    still for vibrations in the sand.
  observationTips: Due to their small size and camouflaged earth tones, look closely
    at the base of large desert rocks or rocky outcroppings where they might be hiding
    in the shadows.
  funFact: Despite being highly dangerous, its potent venom contains a specialized
    peptide called chlorotoxin, which has been utilized in medical research to highlight
    and help eliminate brain tumors.
  facts:
  - Like almost all scorpions, they glow an eerie, bright cyan-blue color when exposed
    to ultraviolet light due to fluorescent chemicals in their exoskeleton.
  - They do not rely on eyesight to hunt; instead, they use tiny, specialized sensory
    hairs on their legs to detect microscopic ground vibrations made by moving insects.
  - They are exceptionally resilient to extreme heat and dehydration, capable of
    slowing their metabolic rate to survive on just a few insects per year.
